# Git & Commit Rules

- Branch naming: `feature/<short-name>`, `fix/<short-name>`, off `main`.
- Never commit directly to `main`.
- Commit format (Conventional Commits):
  `type(scope): short imperative summary`
  Types: `feat`, `fix`, `test`, `docs`, `refactor`, `chore`.
  Example: `feat(auth): add login use case with unit tests`
- One logical change per commit. Do not mix a feature and an unrelated
  formatting pass in the same commit.
- A commit that adds a Bloc/use case without its test is incomplete — it
  should not be proposed as "done" (see `002-testing.mdc`).
